 "description": "cachesplit moved the breakpoint onto the stable half of the system block. The volatile tail does not change between the two requests, so the client body would be read in full too: the split saved nothing. The host's hash of message 1 differs on turn 1 (a cache mark moved onto it) although its text is the same, and the provider read the whole 7,000 tokens. A split is credited only when the client body would have written what the forwarded body read (design \u00a74.4). Here it would not: no split effect, a zero total.",
